# LoadZone Loading UX

- Any navigation, async data dependency, or mutation that may take longer than an instant must show immediate pending feedback when the wait is visible.
- **Staff authenticated shell (`apps/app`):** one initial loader only — empty sidebar slot + empty main card + centered `Spinner`. Do not use multi-block full-page skeletons that mimic a fake dashboard. After first paint, prefer Next.js `Link`/`router.prefetch` on primary nav and keep the painted shell during soft navigations; do not flash route-level page skeletons.
- Prefer `Skeleton` for in-component structural islands (panels, lists, cards) so local layout stays stable; use `Spinner` for compact inline, indeterminate, or the single staff initial-shell wait.
- In App Router, avoid staff segment `loading.tsx` that replaces the whole main column with generic page chrome. Use `Suspense` fallbacks for smaller async islands; player routes may still use route-level `loading.tsx` when appropriate.
- While a request or transition is pending, disable or otherwise guard repeated actions when duplicate taps/clicks would feel broken or trigger duplicate work.
- Never leave blank interactive controls during a visible wait state inside a component the user is acting on.
